   </item>
   <item row="0" column="0">
    <widget class="QLabel" name="leadTimeLabel">
     <property name="toolTip">
      <string>How early, in minutes, the scheduler may start a job. When the next job is due within this time, it starts right away, so slewing, focusing, alignment and guiding are done by the time imaging should begin. When it is due later, the scheduler waits, and parks the mount if the job uses the Track step.</string>
     </property>
     <property name="text">
      <string>Lead time:</string>
     </property>
    </widget>
   </item>
   <item row="2" column="0">
    <widget class="QCheckBox" name="kcfg_PreemptiveShutdown">
     <property name="toolTip">
      <string>If the next job is more than this many hours away, shut the observatory down (park, close ...) and start it up again when the job is due.</string>
     </property>
     <property name="text">
      <string>Pre-emptive shutdown:</string>
     </property>
    </widget>
   </item>
